Article 3-2 (Establishment of Basic Plans for School Meals, etc.)
(1) The Minister of Education shall establish a basic plan for school meals (hereinafter referred to as the “basic plan”) every five years.
(2) The basic plan shall include the following:
1. Goals and basic direction of school meal policy;
2. Matters concerning hygiene, safety, and nutrition management of school meals;
3. Matters concerning nutrition and dietary education and guidance, and nutrition counseling;
4. Matters concerning quality control of food ingredients for school meals;
5. Matters concerning improvement of the school meal system;
6. Matters concerning surveys and research on school meals;
7. Other matters necessary for school meals.
(3) The superintendent of education shall establish and implement an annual implementation plan for school meals based on the basic plan.
(4) Other matters necessary for the establishment and implementation of the basic plan and implementation plans shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

