Article 9 (Support for Expenses Concerning Meals)
(1) The State or a local government may support all or part of the expenses to be borne by guardians under Article 8.
(2) When supporting expenses to be borne by guardians under paragraph (1), priority shall be given to students falling under any of the following categories: <Amended Oct. 17, 2007; Jul. 23, 2010; Mar. 23, 2021; Apr. 28, 2026>
1. Students who, or whose guardians, are persons entitled to benefits under Article 2 of the National Basic Living Security Act or belong to the near-poverty class, and students eligible for support under Articles 5 and 5-2 of the Single-Parent Family Support Act;
2. Students attending schools located in islands and remote areas under Article 2 of the Act on the Promotion of Education in Islands and Remote Areas, or schools in equivalent areas prescribed by Presidential Decree;
3. Students attending agricultural and fishing village schools under Article 3 subparagraph 4 of the Special Act on Improving the Quality of Life of Farmers and Fishers and Promoting Development in Rural Areas, or schools in equivalent areas prescribed by Presidential Decree;
4. Other students deemed necessary by the superintendent of education.
(3) Where a disaster under Article 3 subparagraph 1 of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety makes school meals difficult to provide, the superintendent of education may, following deliberation by the School Meal Committee under Article 5 (1), provide food ingredients and similar support to students' households as prescribed by Presidential Decree. In such cases, the scope of support shall be limited to expenses concerning meals supported by the State or local governments under Article 8 (4) and paragraph (1) of this Article. <Newly Inserted Dec. 28, 2021>

